From e04c286b6ef8233b15e661a4d1b4464d977fb294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:24:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix(trace): keep the set speck size on enlarged working
 grids (ADR-392)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator change: Remove ink specks now keeps and removes the same marks
when a small image traces on a 2x or 3x working grid as it does at native
size. Bilinear enlargement rounds a mark's corners and takes part of a
source pixel off its area (a 3x3 speck keeps 77 of its 81 working pixels
at 3x), so a mark of exactly the set size could vanish on the enlarged
grid. The enlarged test now compares against (N - 1/2) x scale² working
pixels; at native size nothing changes, because pixel counts are whole
numbers. despeckle takes the scale as a named option, so an older call
that passes a connectivity of 4 or 8 in third place no longer
type-checks instead of silently running as a scale.

Measured: despeckle-supersample.test.ts checks marks of 1 to 9 px against
settings 2 to 10 at native size, 2x and 3x; every enlarged result now
matches the native one. Against the same code without the margin, the 48
audit corpus traces and the dragon traces are identical. On the Arch
House logo (2x grid) Smooth keeps one more pale 2-px mark (49 to 50
outlines; 50 on 85ee406 too).

